From: DKR-R Win95 port
Subject: [PATCH] Trace SP and DP edges behind an environment variable

DKR schedules its next task on the SP edge, which makes the interrupt order
observable from inside the game. A crash on Windows 95 shows sc->curRSPTask null
inside __scHandleRSP: the game receives an RSP task completion while it has no
current task.

Reasoning about that sequence without seeing it is guesswork, and this project
already carries six patches about SP and DP completion ordering, which is enough
to say the area resists reasoning.

What the trace established immediately, and what no amount of reading would have:
the crash follows exactly one submission and exactly one SP edge. There is no
duplicate delivery, and adding a delay before publishing the edge changes nothing
-- same fault, same registers -- so it is not a timing race either.

The trace is off unless DKR_TRACE_SP is set, and stops after a few hundred lines.

diff --git a/ultramodern/src/events.cpp b/ultramodern/src/events.cpp
--- a/ultramodern/src/events.cpp
+++ b/ultramodern/src/events.cpp
@@ -256,7 +256,37 @@
     }
 }
 
+// --- Trace des bords SP et DP, activee par DKR_TRACE_SP ------------------------
+//
+// DKR planifie sa tache suivante sur le bord SP, ce qui rend l'ordre des
+// interruptions observable depuis le jeu. Un plantage sur Windows 95 montre
+// `sc->curRSPTask` nul dans `__scHandleRSP` : le jeu recoit une fin de tache RSP
+// alors qu'il n'en a pas en cours.
+//
+// Raisonner sur cette sequence sans la voir revient a deviner, et ce portage
+// porte deja six correctifs sur l'ordre d'achevement SP et DP.
+//
+// La trace s'arrete d'elle-meme apres quelques centaines de lignes : la machine
+// cible ecrit sur une disquette emulee.
+static std::atomic<unsigned> g_trace_submits{0};
+static std::atomic<unsigned> g_trace_sp{0};
+static std::atomic<unsigned> g_trace_dp{0};
+static bool trace_sp_enabled() {
+    static const bool on = (std::getenv("DKR_TRACE_SP") != nullptr);
+    return on;
+}
+static void trace_sp(const char* quoi, unsigned type) {
+    if (!trace_sp_enabled()) { return; }
+    const unsigned n = g_trace_submits.load() + g_trace_sp.load() + g_trace_dp.load();
+    if (n > 400u) { return; }
+    std::fprintf(stderr, "[trace][sp] %-8s type=%u  soumis=%u sp=%u dp=%u\n",
+                 quoi, type, g_trace_submits.load(), g_trace_sp.load(),
+                 g_trace_dp.load());
+}
+
 void sp_complete() {
+    g_trace_sp.fetch_add(1);
+    trace_sp("sp", 0);
     PTR(OSMesgQueue) mq;
     OSMesg msg;
     {
@@ -271,6 +301,8 @@
 }
 
 void dp_complete() {
+    g_trace_dp.fetch_add(1);
+    trace_sp("dp", 0);
     uint8_t* rdram = events_context.rdram;
     ultramodern::lock_guard lock{ events_context.message_mutex };
     ultramodern::enqueue_external_message_src(events_context.dp.mq, events_context.dp.msg, false, ultramodern::EventMessageSource::Dp);
@@ -571,6 +603,8 @@
 
 void ultramodern::submit_rsp_task(RDRAM_ARG PTR(OSTask) task_) {
     OSTask* task = TO_PTR(OSTask, task_);
+    g_trace_submits.fetch_add(1);
+    trace_sp("soumis", task->t.type);
 
     // Send gfx tasks to the graphics action queue
